<article class="env-definition" id="032R">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/032R">Definition <span data-tag="032R">10.162.1</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a ring. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
We say $R$ is <em>universally Japanese</em> if for any finite type ring map $R \to S$ with $S$ a domain we have that $S$ is N-2 (i.e., Japanese). 
</p>
</li><li><p>
We say that $R$ is a <em>Nagata ring</em> if $R$ is Noetherian and for every prime ideal $\mathfrak p$ the ring $R/\mathfrak p$ is N-2. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>